Implements Card 5 of the Behavioral Specification (FormFilla smart
browser form-fill) as a Chrome MV3 extension. The spec was reverse-
engineered from github.com/AhmadHassan-BTed/FormFilla (MIT, 4.7k stars)
per the discovery report — no source code was copied, only the
behavioral spec cards were re-implemented from scratch.

Three-stage pipeline (Card 5 §7.1):
  1. Scanner & Normalizer (src/matching/scanner.ts) — DOM walker that
     extracts 5 signals per field (label, placeholder, name, id, legend)
     and tokenizes them via the abbreviation dictionary.
  2. Hungarian Solver (src/matching/hungarian-solver.ts) — Kuhn-Munkres
     O(n³) on cost = max_score - score, with uniform sentinel padding so
     non-candidate cells never displace real matches.
  3. Framework Setter (src/fill/native-setter.ts) — Native prototype
     setter bypass for React/Vue/Angular, 3-tier fallback chain
     (prototype → plain → pristine-iframe), dispatches input + change
     events with bubbles=true, composed=true, inputType='insertReplacementText'.

Scoring formula (Card 5 §7.2):
  - Exact phrase +35 (×source weight)
  - Regex pattern +20 (×source weight)
  - Fuzzy similarity (max Dice + Jaro-Winkler) × 15 if > 0.6
    (×source weight)
  - Autocomplete token +45 (once)
  - Block context +15 (once)
  - Negative pattern -40 (once)
  Source weights: label 1.0, placeholder 0.9, name 0.8, id 0.7, legend 0.6
  Take max across sources. LOW_THRESHOLD = 30, HIGH_THRESHOLD = 60.

Rules dictionary (Card 5 §7.5):
  rules/rules.json — 18 hotel-guest field rules. Add new rules without
  code changes (the FormFilla extensibility contract).

Chrome MV3 wiring:
  - manifest.json with externally_connectable for workspace UI bridge
  - background.ts — service worker, routes messages, persists guest
  - content.ts — runs on every page, executes fill pipeline on demand
  - popup.html + popup.ts + popup.css — receptionist-facing UI
  - build.mjs — esbuild produces 4 bundles (background.js, content.js,
    popup.js, popup.html+css) + copies rules.json

Workspace UI integration:
  packages/core/components/workspace/workspace-app.tsx — the 'Prepare
  Registration' button now sends the selected guest to the extension
  via chrome.runtime.sendMessage (with window.postMessage fallback
  for dev without the extension installed).

Tests (68 new, 324 workspace-wide):
  - tokenizer.test.ts (14 tests): abbreviation expansion, edge cases
  - similarity.test.ts (16 tests): Dice + Jaro-Winkler + max, symmetry
  - scorer.test.ts (14 tests): every component of Card 5 §7.2, thresholds
  - hungarian-solver.test.ts (11 tests): empty/square/non-square, sentinel
    padding, defensive behaviors, global optimality, 50x50 stress
  - native-setter.test.ts (13 tests): prototype/plain/iframe tiers,
    input/textarea/select/checkbox, event dispatch

Verified:
  - All 324 tests pass workspace-wide (was 256)
  - TypeScript typecheck clean across all 4 packages
  - Next.js production build clean (17 routes + 6 API endpoints)
  - Extension build clean (4 bundles in dist/, total ~25kb)

NOT verified (no Chrome in build env):
  - Live extension load in chrome://extensions
  - End-to-end fill on a real registration form
  The runbook (docs/runbook/extension-form-fill.md) walks through
  loading the extension and running the full demo.

Per owner directive (2026-11-12): implement from the spec cards, do
not copy code from reference repos. The FormFilla source was never
read; only the behavioral spec captured in Card 5 of the Behavioral
Specification document was the contract.
